 "transcript": {
  "language": "en",
  "language_probability": 1.0,
  "duration_seconds": 62.67,
  "segments": [
   {
    "id": "t1",
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 3.18,
    "text": "You ever wondered what the oldest animal is that we've ever discovered?"
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 3.18,
    "end": 5.86,
    "text": "Well, if you haven't, you're definitely wondering it now, so let's talk about it."
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 5.86,
    "end": 7.46,
    "text": "Maybe it's an elephant."
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 7.46,
    "end": 8.88,
    "text": "They live for a long time, right?"
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 8.88,
    "end": 11.34,
    "text": "Or maybe it's a whale. Those also live for a long time."
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 11.34,
    "end": 14.9,
    "text": "Nope, not an elephant or a whale. It's something much, much more exciting."
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "start": 14.9,
    "end": 15.74,
    "text": "Are you ready for this?"
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "start": 15.74,
    "end": 19.18,
    "text": "Behold, the oldest animal ever discovered."
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "start": 19.18,
    "end": 21.6,
    "text": "This clam, whose name is Ming."
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "start": 21.6,
    "end": 25.5,
    "text": "Ming was dredged up by researchers off the coast of Iceland in 2006."
   },
   {
    "id": "t11",
    "start": 25.5,
    "end": 27.58,
    "text": "Now, when they first found him, they just thought Ming was a clam."
   },
   {
    "id": "t12",
    "start": 27.58,
    "end": 29.54,
    "text": "You know, they hadn't made an introduction yet."
   },
   {
    "id": "t13",
    "start": 29.54,
    "end": 32.4,
    "text": "They brought Ming and a bunch of his buddies back to their lab for study."
   },
   {
    "id": "t14",
    "start": 32.4,
    "end": 36.2,
    "text": "Another data point was looking at how old the clams were, which you can actually do fairly easily."
   },
   {
    "id": "t15",
    "start": 36.2,
    "end": 39.2,
    "text": "The clam shells are deposited in layers like tree rings."
   },
   {
    "id": "t16",
    "start": 39.2,
    "end": 41.46,
    "text": "So if you count the layers, you can figure out how old the clam is."
   },
   {
    "id": "t17",
    "start": 41.46,
    "end": 44.66,
    "text": "Fortunately, you can't do this while the clam's alive, so they had to freeze all of them."
   },
   {
    "id": "t18",
    "start": 44.66,
    "end": 49.2,
    "text": "And it was only after that that they sampled Ming and learned that it was 507 years old."
   },
   {
    "id": "t19",
    "start": 49.2,
    "end": 51.26,
    "text": "It'd be really cool to make a discovery like this,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t20",
    "start": 51.26,
    "end": 55.3,
    "text": "but it also come with the realization that you just killed the oldest single individual animal on the planet."
   },
   {
    "id": "t21",
    "start": 55.3,
    "end": 58.6,
    "text": "RIP Ming, 1499-2006, you traded your shells for wings."
   },
   {
    "id": "t22",
    "start": 58.6,
    "end": 59.1,
    "text": "Thanks for watching."
   }
  ]
 },
